      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Scalia.\n(Laughter.)\nQUESTION:\nso that you can answer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d308d4d44a88da894367b357f5f3481ffc79da8b9be633d9c357a795835843bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d308d4d44a88-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Government's arguments, and the amici arguments in particular, rely tremendously on the recidivism rates for felony offenders and felony probationers and fail to point out that in fact the recidivism rate for misdemeanant probationers is substantially lower."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d308d4d44a88da894367b357f5f3481ffc79da8b9be633d9c357a795835843bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d308d4d44a88-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government's consent argument that we started with doesn't save it for the reasons that I suggested earlier."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d308d4d44a88da894367b357f5f3481ffc79da8b9be633d9c357a795835843bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d308d4d44a88-0003-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "represented in its amicus brief that the State has a little over 67,000 police officers and a little over 7,000"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of California",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1260",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d308d4d44a88da894367b357f5f3481ffc79da8b9be633d9c357a795835843bb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d308d4d44a88-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "fact, California has, by conditioning probation on consent to search by any probation officer or law enforcement officer -- the State has, in effect, attempted to enlist its police officers in the administration of the probation program."
    }
